cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "pinn-audit: a controlled audit of PINNs and spectral methods for joint heat inversion"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible computational comparison of physics-informed neural networks
  and spectral inverse methods for recovering a scalar heat diffusivity and an
  unknown initial temperature field from sparse noisy synthetic observations.
  The fixed study varies observation count, initial-field representation and
  neural optimization budget. Results support conditional pipeline comparisons,
  not a universal method-class ranking. Earlier forward-problem work is retained
  as historical material.
authors:
  - family-names: Hasan
    given-names: Ridoy
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
keywords:
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - scientific machine learning
  - partial differential equations
  - reproducibility
